Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner Formation Consistency Evidence Reconciliation Registry

& [RegistryIdentity] is exact
  + [registry_uuid] is f0383dcd-5312-4cc5-8744-77dd2542c98c
  + [profile] is cantor-phase3-topology-scanner-formation-consistency-evidence-reconciliation/0.1
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is f761e445-9961-4a1f-9adc-f973514fd542
  + [requirements] are P3TSFR-001 through P3TSFR-010
  + [state] is registered_unsigned

& [Dispatch] is formation authority retrieval only
  + query current topology scanner evidence vocabulary
  + query dual actual acquisition prerequisites
  + query causal order and common scope
  + query carrier and reconciliation lineage
  + query receipt form, derivation, issuance, consumption, and truth boundaries
  + query prior formation supersession and unchanged scanner policy

& [AuthorityInputs] are exact
  + preserved reconciliation source and processing manifest
  + prior topology scanner formation generation and signature
  + current inventory-consistency evidence and topology form signatures
  + current supplied assembly, digest, and reconciliation signatures
  + physical plan as designed-not-executable boundary

& [RetrievalTerms] include scanner formation reconciliation, InventoryConsistencyEvidence, consistency_evidence, non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal, actual acquisition, complete acquisition, first completion before second start, causal order, common scope, independent carrier lineage, Equal necessary insufficient, pure receipt validity, receipt issuer absence, consumer absence, formation supersession, scanner profile 0.1, and zero physical authority

& [PositiveRouting] returns canonical formation clauses only after replacement signature
& [HistoricalRouting] returns prior formation as superseded historical authority without reinterpretation
& [NegativeRouting] is closed
  + no dispatch exists for production implementation, Windows API, scanner execution, clock read, physical acquisition, fixture, receipt issuance, consumption, admission, mutation, seal, test execution, cleanup, promotion, neural routing, distributed inference, or FPGA execution

& [FaultRouting] is bounded
  + source or predecessor drift routes to governance fault
  + incomplete SJS routes to unsigned authority
  + missing acquisition, order, scope, lineage, or Equal routes to future evidence denial, not current execution
  + unrelated implementation request routes to separate source requirement

& [Status] is pending canonical phase lock and replacement formation signature
